## The Common Writ

wf-law-chapter-reality = Article I: Crimes against Reality
wf-law-chapter-persons = Article II: Crimes against persons and vessels
wf-law-chapter-bench = Article III: Crimes against the Bench
wf-law-chapter-central = Article IV: Ordinances of Caelestinus Central

wf-law-anchor-breach = Breach of the Anchors
wf-law-anchor-breach-text = Raising a hand, weapon or tool against an anchor, its shield or its wardens, or cutting the power to a sanctioned relay.
wf-law-trespass = Trespass beyond the Anchors
wf-law-trespass-text = Entering Dissonance or Feedback space without a Coda Writ.
wf-law-deep-trespass = Trespass in the Coda
wf-law-deep-trespass-text = Entering the Coda without a Bench-sanctioned expedition.
wf-law-unsanctioned-landing = Unsanctioned Landing
wf-law-unsanctioned-landing-text = Entering orbit around, or landing on, a world the Bench has not sanctioned.
wf-law-quarantine-breach = Quarantine Breach
wf-law-quarantine-breach-text = Landing on a quarantine world, or carrying anything off one.
wf-law-unlawful-possession = Possession of Unlawful Material
wf-law-unlawful-possession-text = Holding unlawful material for personal use: a shard, a charm, a token.
wf-law-unlawful-trafficking = Trafficking in Unlawful Material
wf-law-unlawful-trafficking-text = Mining, refining, selling, carrying in bulk or fitting unlawful material to a vessel.
wf-law-artifact = Harbouring an Artifact
wf-law-artifact-text = Keeping, powering or wiring into a vessel any unregistered object recovered beyond the anchors.
wf-law-sedition = Sedition against the Anchors
wf-law-sedition-text = Preaching the unmooring of the sector, or belonging to any congregation that does.

wf-law-murder = Murder
wf-law-murder-text = Unlawfully killing a person.
wf-law-assault = Assault
wf-law-assault-text = Unlawfully harming a person.
wf-law-piracy = Piracy
wf-law-piracy-text = Harpooning, pinning, boarding or stripping a vessel without its crew's consent.
wf-law-hull-theft = Hull Theft
wf-law-hull-theft-text = Flying, selling or breaking a vessel without its deed, or dealing in its parts.

wf-law-heave-to = Failing to Heave To
wf-law-heave-to-text = Ignoring or fleeing a judge's hail.
wf-law-contempt = Contempt of the Bench
wf-law-contempt-text = Attacking or impersonating a judge, or escaping their custody.
wf-law-false-distress = False Distress
wf-law-false-distress-text = Sending a distress call where there is none.
wf-law-warheads = Unsanctioned Warheads
wf-law-warheads-text = Arming a warhead without the authority of a faction's command in time of declared war.

wf-law-brandishing = Brandishing
wf-law-brandishing-text = Carrying a weapon drawn, unholstered or unbagged aboard Central.
wf-law-discharge = Discharge
wf-law-discharge-text = Firing a weapon aboard Central.
wf-law-neutral-ground = Breach of Neutral Ground
wf-law-neutral-ground-text = Waging faction war aboard Central, or within its sanctuary.
wf-law-docking = Docking Order
wf-law-docking-text = Docking against the dockmaster's word, or keeping ship weapons hot within the sanctuary.
wf-law-undeclared = Undeclared Material
wf-law-undeclared-text = Failing to declare unlawful material on docking. Charged together with Article I.
wf-law-concealment = Concealment
wf-law-concealment-text = Refusing to show identification to a judge.

wf-penalty-citation = Citation
wf-penalty-impound = Impound
wf-penalty-banishment = Banishment
wf-penalty-outlawry = Outlawry

contraband-examine-text-WFUnlawful = [color=#b040e0]This is unlawful material under the Common Writ. Surrender it to the Bench.[/color]
